3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Some material here is not ours to license:

  - Figures from OpenStax Anatomy and Physiology 2e (c) Rice University,
    under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Stored as
    anatomy-physiology/figures/os-*.jpg; each is credited where it appears and listed on anatomy-physiology/credits.html.
    OpenStax and Rice University do not endorse LevlPrep.
  - The 3D body model (nremt/assets/body3d.glb), built from BodyParts3D,
    (c) 2008 Life Science Integrated Database Center, under CC BY-SA 2.1
    Japan. The model and any adaptation of it stay under that licence.
  - three.js (nremt/assets/vendor/three/), (c) three.js authors, MIT.
  - Lung-sound recordings (wheeze, crackles, stridor) by James Heilman, MD;
    the stridor clip processed by Natural Philo. CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported,
    streamed from Wikimedia Commons and credited on the sound trainer page.
  - IBM Plex Mono and Nunito, served from assets/fonts/, under the SIL Open
    Font License 1.1.

Neither licence above extends to those.


4. NOT A LICENCE TO PRACTISE
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing here is medical advice or a clinical protocol. It is study material
for an exam. Your own protocols and medical direction are the authority, and
they override anything written here.
